    "show_share": true,
    "description": "December 10 2019 marks the 71st anniversary of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR), a document that was signed and adopted in \n       Paris in 1948  by United Nations (UN) member states. Considered a \"milestone document,\" the Declaration is universal in nature, signifying that the rights and freedoms specified within apply to communities and peoples of all countries and backgrounds. Accordingly, \n       Article 1  states, \"Everyone is entitled to all the rights and freedoms set forth in this Declaration, without distinction of any kind, such as race, colour, sex, language, religion, political or other opinion, national or social origin, property, birth or other status.\"",
